# UST.G3CO: Pole-Six Automatic Open-Arc Exactness Theorem

## Direct finite map

Let `delta=(9,1,3)` and let

```text
M_delta(a): direct_sum_i S_(delta-deg partial_i Phi)
             -> S_delta
```

send ten coefficient polynomials to their contraction with the ten original
Jacobian generators of `Phi(a)`.  Exact enumeration gives

```text
target rows             208,570
coefficient columns     602,597
base nonzero entries 53,850,259.
```

The certified B89 quotient in this degree has dimension zero.  Hence
`M_delta(0)` has full row rank 208,570 at the selected good reduction and in
characteristic zero.

## Automatic exactness

Choose any nonzero maximal B89 minor.  Along the affine G3BI family its
determinant is a nonzero polynomial `Delta_delta(a)` over `Q(gamma)`, because
`Delta_delta(0)` is nonzero.  Every zero is algebraic.  Every interior G3BJ
path value is transcendental, so no such value can be a zero.  The terminal
B89 value `a=0` is also a unit by construction.

Therefore, for every `0<t<=1`,

```text
rank M_delta(a(t)) = 208,570
```

and every selected pole-six source has an exact rational finite right inverse.
This is the requested automatic finite-cutoff exactness at the algebraic
pole-six layer: the finite projected quotient is the exact object, not a
numerical truncation with an unknown tail.

